From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:52:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(open-items): import a session's chat labels into the
 store

Sessions older than the store, or run by an agent without the open_items
tools, have their items only as chat labels. The panel lists those as
"chat only", but nothing stores them, so they miss the stored list's state
and an agent with the tools can be handed a label the chat already uses.

POST /v1/sessions/{id}/open-items/import (edit access) stores items under
the labels they carry, as an agent's adoption does, so the session's
counters move past them; an optional resolution stores an item closed by a
person. A label already stored gets label_taken, and a retry with the same
idempotency key returns what the first attempt stored. The panel offers
"Import N from chat" to editors when the chat has labels the store lacks:
each with its title and block from the chat, closed with the chat's closing
sentence or as dismissed, and pinned links with their URL. Labels of other
letters stay chat only. Nothing is imported unless a person asks.

Not proposed upstream yet: the store it extends is not upstream either.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
